{
  "kanda": "aranya",
  "sarga": 41,
  "title": "Maareecha dissuades Ravana",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga41/aranyasans41.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga41/aranyaitrans41.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Maareecha dissuades Ravana again and warns him of the fatal consequences if Rama is irked by the wrongdoings of Ravana. In every utterance, Maareecha repeats that not only Ravana but the entire demonic race is also going to ruin due to Ravana's impertinence. Finally when Ravana is heedless of these advises, Maareecha prepares himself to die by the arrow of an enemy, namely Rama, rather than by his own clansman, Ravana."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये अरण्य काण्डे एक चत्वारिंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 41st chapter in Aranya Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3.41.1",
      "label": "3.41.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "आज्ञप्तो रावणेन इत्थम् प्रतिकूलम् च राजवत् |\nअब्रवीत् परुषम् वाक्यम् निःशन्को राक्षसाधिपम्",
      "iast": "āapto rāvaṇena ittham pratikūlam ca rājavat |\nabravīt paruṣam vākyam niḥśanko rākṣasādhipam",
